.TH NETSCOPE 1 "" "netscope" "NetScope Manual"
.SH NAME
netscope \- NetScope — from raw network measurements to 'what's wrong, and where', with evidence.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B netscope
.IR command " [ " options " ]"
.br
.B netscope
.B \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
NetScope — from raw network measurements to 'what's wrong, and where', with evidence.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
show this help message and exit
.TP
.B \-\-version
show netscope's version and exit
.SH COMMANDS
.SS diagnose
run a diagnostic round (gateway/DNS/CDN checks) and report the result
.P
\fBnetscope diagnose\fR [\-v] [\-\-gateway \fIGATEWAY\fR] [\-\-json]
.P
.TP
.B \-\-verbose, \-v
enable verbose (INFO\-level) logging
.TP
.B \-\-gateway \fIGATEWAY\fR
gateway to probe: an IP, 'auto' (detect from the OS, default), or 'none' (skip the gateway check)
.TP
.B \-\-json
output machine\-readable JSON instead of styled text
.SS check
probe one target with any subset of the service checks and report the result
.P
\fBnetscope check\fR \fITARGET\fR [\-v] [\-\-checks \fICHECKS\fR] [\-\-json]
.P
.TP
.B \-\-verbose, \-v
enable verbose (INFO\-level) logging
.TP
.B \-\-checks \fICHECKS\fR
comma\-separated subset of checks to run (default: all five)
.TP
.B \-\-json
output machine\-readable JSON instead of styled text
.SS route
trace the route to a target and report route stability
.P
\fBnetscope route\fR \fITARGET\fR [\-v] [\-\-no\-resolve] [\-\-json]
.P
.TP
.B \-\-verbose, \-v
enable verbose (INFO\-level) logging
.TP
.B \-\-no\-resolve
skip reverse\-DNS hostname resolution for hops
.TP
.B \-\-json
output machine\-readable JSON instead of styled text
.SS history
show recent measurement rounds from the local log
.P
\fBnetscope history\fR [\-v] [\-\-limit \fILIMIT\fR] [\-\-json]
.P
.TP
.B \-\-verbose, \-v
enable verbose (INFO\-level) logging
.TP
.B \-\-limit \fILIMIT\fR
maximum number of rounds to show (default: 20)
.TP
.B \-\-json
output machine\-readable JSON instead of styled text
.SS monitor
run continuous measurement rounds with incident detection (Ctrl+C to stop)
.P
\fBnetscope monitor\fR [\-v] [\-\-interval \fIINTERVAL\fR] [\-\-rounds \fIROUNDS\fR] [\-\-gateway \fIGATEWAY\fR]
.P
.TP
.B \-\-verbose, \-v
enable verbose (INFO\-level) logging
.TP
.B \-\-interval \fIINTERVAL\fR
seconds between rounds (default: 30)
.TP
.B \-\-rounds \fIROUNDS\fR
number of rounds before stopping (0 = until Ctrl+C)
.TP
.B \-\-gateway \fIGATEWAY\fR
gateway to probe: an IP, 'auto', or 'none'
.SS speed
measure download throughput (median Mbps over a sampling window)
.P
\fBnetscope speed\fR [\-v] [\-\-url \fIURL\fR] [\-\-seconds \fISECONDS\fR] [\-\-json]
.P
.TP
.B \-\-verbose, \-v
enable verbose (INFO\-level) logging
.TP
.B \-\-url \fIURL\fR
download URL to measure (default: the bandwidth_url config key)
.TP
.B \-\-seconds \fISECONDS\fR
measurement window in seconds (default: the bandwidth_seconds config key)
.TP
.B \-\-json
output machine\-readable JSON instead of styled text
.SS report
export a self\-contained evidence report from the local measurement log (markdown, or \-\-json)
.P
\fBnetscope report\fR [\-v] [\-\-days \fIDAYS\fR] [\-\-target \fITARGET\fR] [\-\-out \fIOUT\fR] [\-\-html \fIFILE\fR] [\-\-json]
.P
.TP
.B \-\-verbose, \-v
enable verbose (INFO\-level) logging
.TP
.B \-\-days \fIDAYS\fR
window length in days, ending now (default: 7)
.TP
.B \-\-target \fITARGET\fR
restrict the report to one target (default: every target in the window)
.TP
.B \-\-out \fIOUT\fR
write the markdown report to a file (UTF\-8) instead of stdout
.TP
.B \-\-html \fIFILE\fR
write a self\-contained HTML report (dark theme, inline SVG trends) to FILE (UTF\-8); ignored under \-\-json
.TP
.B \-\-json
output machine\-readable JSON instead of markdown
.SS service
manage the saved service list (persisted locally; shared by the CLI and the TUI services board)
.P
\fBnetscope service\fR \fISERVICE_COMMAND\fR [\-v]
.P
.TP
.B \-\-verbose, \-v
enable verbose (INFO\-level) logging
.SS service add
save (or update) a service in the curated list
.P
\fBnetscope service add\fR \fINAME\fR \fIHOST\fR [\-\-checks \fICHECKS\fR]
.P
.TP
.B \-\-checks \fICHECKS\fR
comma\-separated subset of checks to enable (default: all five)
.SS service list
list the saved services
.P
\fBnetscope service list\fR [\-\-json]
.P
.TP
.B \-\-json
output machine\-readable JSON instead of styled text
.SS service remove
remove a service from the saved list
.P
\fBnetscope service remove\fR \fINAME\fR
.P
.SS service check
run a saved service's checks now and report the result
.P
\fBnetscope service check\fR \fINAME\fR [\-\-json]
.P
.TP
.B \-\-json
output machine\-readable JSON instead of styled text
.SS completions
print a shell completion script to stdout, ready for the shell's completion directory
.P
\fBnetscope completions\fR \fISHELL\fR [\-v]
.P
.TP
.B \-\-verbose, \-v
enable verbose (INFO\-level) logging
.SS tui
launch the live terminal dashboard (requires: pip install netscope[tui])
.P
\fBnetscope tui\fR [\-v]
.P
.TP
.B \-\-verbose, \-v
enable verbose (INFO\-level) logging
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
success; the evidence is printed even when the diagnosis reports a problem
.TP
.B 1
runtime failure, e.g. `netscope tui` without its extra installed
.TP
.B 2
usage error (unknown command, bad option value)
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.netscope/config.toml
optional user configuration
.TP
.I ~/.netscope/netscope.db
local SQLite log: measurements, baselines, route history, saved services
.TP
.I ~/.netscope/ipasn.dat
optional offline ASN database; enables AS numbers in `netscope route`
